# Project Knowledge

<!--
  This file is the contract between your project's stack and the Claude Kit
  Plan/Review stages. The kit defaults to language-neutral behavior when slots
  are unfilled (the plan-reviewer SKIPs the corresponding check and emits a
  consolidated NIT issue listing skipped slots).

  Cascade order (highest precedence first):
    1. PROJECT-KNOWLEDGE.md (this file)
    2. CLAUDE.md Language Profile section (kit default — legacy fallback)
    3. Abstract default — the check is SKIPPED

  Fill in the slots below for full architecture validation. Run
  /project-researcher to auto-generate values from your codebase, or fill
  manually.

  Slot consumers:
    - /planner reads this file at startup step 1.5
    - plan-reviewer gets these slots injected via additionalContext
      by .claude/scripts/inject-review-context.sh (SubagentStart hook)
-->

## Language Profile

- LANGUAGE: <your-language>            # e.g. go, python, typescript, java, rust
- LANG_EXT: <your-extension>           # e.g. .go, .py, .ts, .java, .rs
- VERIFY_CMD: <your-verify-command>    # full lint+test+vet pipeline; e.g. `make verify`
- BUILD_CMD: <your-build-command>      # e.g. `make build`, `npm run build`, `cargo build`
- TEST_CMD: <your-test-command>        # e.g. `make test`, `pytest`, `npm test`
- LINT_CMD: <your-lint-command>        # e.g. `make lint`, `ruff check`, `eslint`
- FMT_CMD: <your-format-command>       # e.g. `gofmt -w {}`, `black {}`, `make fmt`. Use `{}`
                                       # placeholder for per-file mode (auto-fmt.sh substitutes
                                       # the changed file path). Without `{}`, runs as-is
                                       # (whole-project formatter).
- DEPENDENCY_FILE: <your-dep-file>     # manifest used to declare external libraries; one of:
                                       # Go:        go.mod
                                       # Python:    pyproject.toml (or requirements.txt for legacy)
                                       # TypeScript: package.json
                                       # Rust:      Cargo.toml
                                       # Java:      pom.xml (Maven) or build.gradle (Gradle)
- INSTALL_VERB: <your-install-cmd>     # command to install a new declared dependency; one of:
                                       # Go:        go get
                                       # Python:    pip install (or poetry add)
                                       # TypeScript: npm install (or yarn add, pnpm add)
                                       # Rust:      cargo add
                                       # Java:      mvn dependency:get (or gradle dependencies)

## Source Layout

- SOURCE_GLOB: <your-source-glob>      # e.g. `internal/**/*.go`, `src/**/*.py`
- TEST_GLOB: <your-test-glob>          # e.g. `**/*_test.go`, `tests/**/*.py`
- GENERATED_PATTERN: <your-gen-glob>   # files protected from edit; e.g. `*_gen.go`, `*.pb.go`
- MOCK_PATTERN: <your-mock-glob>       # e.g. `*/mocks/*.go`, `*.mock.ts`

## Architecture (Layer Vocabulary)

- ARCHITECTURE_STYLE: <your-style>     # one of: layered | flat | event_driven | hexagonal | other
                                       # layered      — explicit dependency layers (LAYERS + LAYER_RULE define them)
                                       # flat         — single module, no enforced layer ordering
                                       # event_driven — events / handlers / sagas; LAYER_RULE check N/A
                                       # hexagonal    — core + adapters; LAYERS may be [core, adapters] or unset
                                       # other        — declared but not modeled; planner asks ad-hoc
                                       #
                                       # Default if unset: behaves as if "layered" was set IF LAYERS is also
                                       # populated; else behaves as if "other" (SKIP layer-related checks with
                                       # consolidated NIT). This preserves backwards-compat: existing PK files
                                       # with LAYERS populated continue working without adding this slot.

- LAYERS:                              # ordered list, lower → higher
                                       # Required when ARCHITECTURE_STYLE = layered.
                                       # Optional otherwise (planner / reviewer SKIP layer checks).
  - <data-access-layer>                # e.g. repository, dao, persistence
  - <business-layer>                   # e.g. service, usecase, controller
  - <api-layer>                        # e.g. handler, view, endpoint
- LAYER_RULE: |
    <describe import-direction rules in your project; e.g.>
    - <api-layer> imports <business-layer>; NEVER imports <data-access-layer> directly
    - <business-layer> imports <data-access-layer>
    - <data-access-layer> imports models only

## Domain Purity

- DOMAIN_PROHIBIT: <pattern-or-rule>   # what MUST NOT appear in domain entities
                                       # examples:
                                       # Go:        no encoding/json struct tags (no `json:` or `db:`)
                                       # Python:    no sqlalchemy / django.db imports
                                       # TypeScript: no class-validator / TypeORM decorators
                                       # Java:      no @Entity / @Column annotations on records

## Error Handling

- ERROR_WRAP: <wrap-pattern>           # how errors are propagated with context
                                       # examples:
                                       # Go:        fmt.Errorf("context: %w", err)
                                       # Python:    raise XError("context") from err
                                       # TypeScript: throw new XError("context", { cause: err })
                                       # Java:      throw new XException("context", err)

## Configuration

- CONFIG_EXAMPLE: <path>               # e.g. config.yaml.example, .env.example
- CONFIG_DOCS: <path>                  # e.g. README.md, docs/configuration.md

## Concurrency (optional)

- CONCURRENCY_PRIMITIVES: <list>       # e.g. goroutines+channels (Go), asyncio+task (Python),
                                       # Promise+worker (TypeScript), virtual threads (Java)
- CONCURRENCY_LEAKS: <leak-name>       # e.g. goroutine leak, unawaited task, dangling Promise
